=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play firewall/active22 ---------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: firewall/active22$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. ufw active, default deny$
# incoming, allowing 22, where sshd listens.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Disable Firewall #############################################$
$
# Warning$
# This stops the firewall and leaves every port open.$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
$
   -  Disable ufw$
      ufw$
      -active$
      +inactive$
      $ ufw disable$
$
  Disable the firewall? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Disable ufw          Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [ ] Firewall             Not Configured inactive$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [ ] Status               Inactive$
   -  Incoming policy      Deny$
  [ ] At boot              No$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  [::]:22              Not filtered$
   -  0.0.0.0:22           Not filtered$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  22/tcp               Allow Saved$
   -  22/tcp (v6)          Allow Saved$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable firewall      Let SSH through, then start ufw$
                           [ ] Lockout risk$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: firewall/active22$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Disable ufw$
      $ ufw disable$
$

